# Files and folders that chezmoi deletes from your home folder when it applies
# the dotfiles, if they exist. Each line is a path in your home folder, written
# without the ~/. (This file is read as a template, like .chezmoiignore.)
#
# chezmoi stops managing a file that is deleted from this repository, but it
# leaves the copy that is already in your home folder. Listing the file here
# deletes that copy too, on every machine's next `chezmoi update`.

# Earlier versions of these dotfiles configured zsh; the shell setup now lives
# in fish (~/.config/fish). These are the files those versions wrote. On a Mac,
# the same apply writes the new ~/.zprofile, which isn't listed here. Your own
# files are left alone: ~/.config/zsh/.zshrc.local (install.sh reminds you to
# move it to fish) and zsh's history in ~/.local/state/zsh.
.zshenv
.config/zsh/.zshenv
.config/zsh/.zprofile
.config/zsh/.zshrc
.config/zsh/.zlogin
.config/zsh/.zlogout
.config/zsh/completions
.config/zsh/themes
.cache/zsh

# fish files these dotfiles no longer ship, so that fish's own behaviour comes
# back everywhere: fish_user_key_bindings.fish replaced what Up and Down do. To
# put your own file at one of these paths later, delete its line here first, or
# chezmoi deletes the file again on every apply.
.config/fish/functions/fish_user_key_bindings.fish
